  "title": "Apple's Defense of Google Search Deal in Court",
  "summary": "Apple's defense in the US v. Google antitrust trial includes arguments about user experience, privacy, and the necessity of Google's services in Apple's ecosystem.",
  "tags": ["Apple", "Google", "Search Engine", "Antitrust Trial", "User Experience", "Privacy"],
  "body": "<p>Apple's defense in the US v. Google antitrust trial includes arguments about user experience, privacy, and the necessity of Google's services in Apple's ecosystem. Key points include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Apple argues against offering users a choice of search engines during setup due to the potential for a poor user experience.</li>\n<li>Apple maintains that Google is the best search engine and has better privacy practices compared to competitors.</li>\n<li>Apple emphasizes the seamless integration of Google services into its platform, citing historical innovations like the URL and search bar combination in Safari.</li>\n</ul>"
}
